{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0179owFfaAZ3THhdkSHPEp7N","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# docs/: what counsel reads\n2\t\n3\tThe method rules, briefs and rulings that govern this repository as its own tenant, at the version the manifest's `[counsel].reads` names. Counsel is handed these paths before it answers (`ATTAVO_COUNSEL_READS`); a path named in the manifest that does not exist is refused, not skipped. The living copies of the operator's documents are kept elsewhere; what is here is what a record may cite, and a citation into `docs/` resolves to a file in the repository at the record's commit.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ee75ad-edac-4244-be61-f864406c706c","uuid":"153fbdf1-6a06-4134-9b9e-144ba1eb866b","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:48:49.259Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-277/attest/specs/277/stub/docs/README.md","content":"# docs/: what counsel reads\n\nThe method rules, briefs and rulings that govern this repository as its own tenant, at the version the manifest's `[counsel].reads` names. Counsel is handed these paths before it answers (`ATTAVO_COUNSEL_READS`); a path named in the manifest that does not exist is refused, not skipped. The living copies of the operator's documents are kept elsewhere; what is here is what a record may cite, and a citation into `docs/` resolves to a file in the repository at the record's commit.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
