{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PyhVHCtm9FFnRfQoyKsae3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The three stores: where a thing lives (ruled 2026-09-25)\n2\t\n3\tOne test decides the store: does the attestation bind to it?\n4\t\n5\t1. **Git**: facts and policy the attestation binds to. The spec and its criteria; approval bound to the spec's sha; invocation markers; build, review, counsel and ruling records; the manifest, including policy such as `[operators].approvers` (a claim the attestation makes, so a tenant must be able to prove it with the repository alone). Small, versioned, travels with the branch, survives the product.\n6\t2. **The product's datastore**: state and working material the attestation does not bind to. Identity state; indexes over git (ledger, measurements, report caches, legitimate only as caches rebuilt from git); the Plan area's working documents; the per-item conversation. A Plan document a spec's research record or a ruling cites is copied into `docs/` in the tenant at its cited version in the same commit as the citation.\n7\t3. **Content-addressed bulk**: bytes a fact points at by hash: build logs, events files, later any executor evidence. The record carries `log_sha256` and a locator; the attestation binds to the hash. The backend is the tenant's declaration in the manifest, offered in this order: git LFS (keeps \"verify with the repository alone\" true), the tenant's own object store behind a `put`/`get` command pair, GitHub release assets. GitHub Actions artifacts are not a candidate: they expire.\n8\t\n9\t## Consequences\n10\t\n11\t- Records are never moved to a datastore to save repository size; they are not the size.\n12\t- First step: every build, verify and counsel record carries `log_sha256`, computed at write time, with the log still in git; one field that turns every later move into a change of locator, not of attestation. Beside it, two measurements at retire: repository size per item and log bytes per attempt; they say when to declare a bulk backend.\n13\t- The index over git is built when a doctor or report read is slow enough to move a decision.\n14\t- Counsel's corpus belongs in the repository under `docs/`; `[counsel].reads` names it.\n15\t- Auth and RBAC: policy in git (the manifest), identity delegated to the forge, state in the datastore.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ee75ad-edac-4244-be61-f864406c706c","uuid":"33468343-3452-4714-be5f-2631b6f05a85","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:48:57.125Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-277/attest/specs/277/stub/docs/storage-ruling.md","content":"# The three stores: where a thing lives (ruled 2026-09-25)\n\nOne test decides the store: does the attestation bind to it?\n\n1. **Git**: facts and policy the attestation binds to. The spec and its criteria; approval bound to the spec's sha; invocation markers; build, review, counsel and ruling records; the manifest, including policy such as `[operators].approvers` (a claim the attestation makes, so a tenant must be able to prove it with the repository alone). Small, versioned, travels with the branch, survives the product.\n2. **The product's datastore**: state and working material the attestation does not bind to. Identity state; indexes over git (ledger, measurements, report caches, legitimate only as caches rebuilt from git); the Plan area's working documents; the per-item conversation. A Plan document a spec's research record or a ruling cites is copied into `docs/` in the tenant at its cited version in the same commit as the citation.\n3. **Content-addressed bulk**: bytes a fact points at by hash: build logs, events files, later any executor evidence. The record carries `log_sha256` and a locator; the attestation binds to the hash. The backend is the tenant's declaration in the manifest, offered in this order: git LFS (keeps \"verify with the repository alone\" true), the tenant's own object store behind a `put`/`get` command pair, GitHub release assets. GitHub Actions artifacts are not a candidate: they expire.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Records are never moved to a datastore to save repository size; they are not the size.\n- First step: every build, verify and counsel record carries `log_sha256`, computed at write time, with the log still in git; one field that turns every later move into a change of locator, not of attestation. Beside it, two measurements at retire: repository size per item and log bytes per attempt; they say when to declare a bulk backend.\n- The index over git is built when a doctor or report read is slow enough to move a decision.\n- Counsel's corpus belongs in the repository under `docs/`; `[counsel].reads` names it.\n- Auth and RBAC: policy in git (the manifest), identity delegated to the forge, state in the datastore.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}}}
