{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9cjW64jqz2s7xr8Fx1jqV","type":"tool_result","content":"205\trerun -- without spending a second on it; --fresh reruns anyway. A\n206\tfailing run is never cached, since the next question after one is always\n207\twhether an edit fixed it. [tests].exclude_in_executor names test\n208\tidentifiers left out, and said so, when ATTAVO_STAGE is set (inside an\n209\texecutor); they run outside one and in CI. When ATTAVO_EVENTS is set, one\n210\tevent of kind test is written per invocation, naming the mode, the count\n211\tselected, the exit code, and the seconds spent (or that the answer came\n212\tfrom the cache). It is the one test command an executor is given (issue\n213\t#212); the product's own transport -- drive, worker, build, verify,\n214\tcounsel, file-stops -- refuses to run at all when ATTAVO_STAGE is set,\n215\tsince the transport is the pass's, not the executor's.\n216\t\n217\tverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\n218\tstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\n219\ta tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\n220\tline per check as \"<name> <conclusion>\". verify runs it on the build\n221\trecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\n222\tskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\n223\tadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\n224\tcalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\n225\t[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\n226\tthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\n227\tfindings and its declared \"reports\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\n228\tbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\n229\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\n230\tresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\n231\tcarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\n232\tcarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\n233\tthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\n234\trefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\n235\tretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\n236\tfull rules both enforce.\n237\t\n238\tfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\n239\tissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\n240\tclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\n241\tlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\n242\tbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\n243\tfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\n244\tthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\n245\tcommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\n246\tnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\n247\tempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\n248\tcould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n249\t\n250\tcounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\n251\twhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\n252\tpoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\n253\tapproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\n254\t[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\n255\tread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\n256\tclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\n257\titem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\n258\troot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\n259\tsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\n260\tstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\n261\tcitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\n262\tdiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\n263\t(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\n264\tand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\n265\tthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\n266\ttranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\n267\tcaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\n268\twritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\n269\trecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\n270\tenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\n271\t\n272\trecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\n273\tpaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\n274\tcheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\n275\tguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\n276\tcopy of the check.\n277\t\n278\tattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\n279\tverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ee75ad-edac-4244-be61-f864406c706c","uuid":"6c7c1f95-97f5-4344-a4a0-5a6d8c3a8b87","timestamp":"2026-10-01T19:51:16.899Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-277/attavo/cli.py","content":"rerun -- without spending a second on it; --fresh reruns anyway. A\nfailing run is never cached, since the next question after one is always\nwhether an edit fixed it. [tests].exclude_in_executor names test\nidentifiers left out, and said so, when ATTAVO_STAGE is set (inside an\nexecutor); they run outside one and in CI. When ATTAVO_EVENTS is set, one\nevent of kind test is written